{"name":"Nero","hex":"#252525","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Nero","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Roman Emperor from 54 to 68, and the last Emperor of the Julio-Claudian dynasty.","An agnomen first held by Tiberius Claudius Nero, an ancestor of Tiberius, Caligula, Claudius and Nero."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any cruel and wicked tyrant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Nero"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nero","blocks":[{"text":"Nero was Roman emperor from AD 54 until his suicide in AD 68, as the final emperor of the Julio-Claudian dynasty."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Nero_Glyptothek_Munich_321.jpg/330px-Nero_Glyptothek_Munich_321.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nero","wikidata":"Q1413"},{"title":"Nero (Devil May Cry)","blocks":[{"text":"Nero  is a character in Devil May Cry, an action-adventure game series by Japanese developer and publisher Capcom. He is the nephew of original Devil May Cry protagonist Dante, and the son of recurring series antagonist Vergil. He first appeared in Devil May Cry 4 as the primary protagonist. Nero, a teenager who works for the Order of the Sword, uses demonic powers inherited from Sparda to hunt demons. Nero returns as the primary protagonist in Devil May Cry 5 to fight the demon king Urizen, a new threat. He has also appeared in printed media related to these two games. He is portrayed in voice acting and motion capture by Johnny Yong Bosch."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/01/NeroDevilMayCry5.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nero_(Devil_May_Cry)","wikidata":"Q1217094"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Great_Cameo_of_France-removebg.png/330px-Great_Cameo_of_France-removebg.png?utm_source=en.wikiped